<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	P6 "Share extensions" task (plan §Platform parity). Share extensions run
	in their own sandboxed process, separate from `Enchiridion2Mac` — this
	entitlement is what lets `Enchiridion2MacShareExtension` resolve the SAME
	App Group container as the host app via
	`FileManager.containerURL(forSecurityApplicationGroupIdentifier:)`, and
	therefore write into the same on-disk `LocalGraphStore` SQLite file
	(`EnchiridionShareKit`'s `ShareCapture.captureIntoAppGroupStore`) that the
	main app and both widget extensions already share. Identifier must match
	`EnchiridionMac.entitlements`/`EnchiridionMacWidget.entitlements` exactly
	— see those files' comments for the full rationale.
	App extensions are sandboxed by default on macOS (Apple requires
	`APPLICATION_EXTENSION_API_ONLY`, already set in project.yml). Unlike the
	widget extension (read-only, no network keys needed), this extension
	writes to the local App Group container only — still no network access
	of its own (capture is local-write-only; see `EnchiridionShareKit`'s
	README for why image/attachment capture, which WOULD eventually need
	network access for an R2 upload, is out of scope for this task).
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.dev.rawkode.enchiridion2</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
